<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down in limited trade.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down in limited trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell 50-100 rupees per tonne on Monday in limited trade as most markets in central India were closed for a Moslem festival, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady and business volumes low.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were also steady in limited transactions.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was quoted at $276-277 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was offered at $110 rupees per tonne for ready shipment and $105 per tonne for March-April shipment. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at 3,750 rupees (f.o.r) Bedibunder for ready delivery and at 3,650 rupees per tonne (f.o.r) March-April delivery.</p>
<p>The undertone was steady.</p>
